# Wizard create warm ownership

## Problem

`warmOperatorWizardShell(pluginId)` awaits `ensureWizardHostReady` → workspace
`wizardHost.ensureReady`. Denali historically warmed **create + flat-edit + shared**
UI surfaces in one `Promise.all`, so `/tours/new` paid for flat-edit-only chunks:

- `wizard-flat-edit-chrome-surface`
- `wizard-flat-edit-form-surface`
- `wizard-flat-edit-page-surface`

## Decision (ownership split)

| Path | Warm entry | Surfaces owned |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create `/tours/new` | `warmOperatorWizardShell` → `wizardHost.ensureReady` only | host-adapter, createChrome, createView, operatorUi, labels, wizardSurfaces (composite+review) |
| Flat-edit `…/tours/[id]/edit` | `warmOperatorWizardShell` **then** `ensureFlatEditChromeReady` + `ensureFlatEditFormReady` + `ensureFlatEditPageReady` | same shared set **plus** the three flat-edit Pattern B surfaces |

### Non-goals

- No change to SDK capability **shape** (`flatEditChrome|Form|Page.ensureReady` remain).
- No change to `warmOperatorWizardShell` API.
- No change to create/draft lifecycle or createView/createChrome contracts.
- Flat-edit package `ensure*` stay idempotent (cache hit returns existing surface).

### Contract notes

- `wizardHost.ensureReady` must **not** import flat-edit UI surfaces (create must stay lean).
- Flat-edit page client must not mount Ready until the three flat-edit peeks are non-null
  (or equivalent ensures completed). Cached plugin from create warm alone is insufficient.
- Capability bag still exposes per-surface `ensureReady` for on-demand / edit callers.

## Before / after dependency graph

```text
BEFORE (create = edit warm set)
warmOperatorWizardShell
  └─ wizardHost.ensureReady
       ├─ host-adapter
       ├─ createChrome + createView
       ├─ flatEditChrome + flatEditForm + flatEditPage   ← create paid this
       ├─ operatorUi + labels + wizardSurfaces

AFTER
warmOperatorWizardShell (/tours/new)
  └─ wizardHost.ensureReady
       ├─ host-adapter
       ├─ createChrome + createView
       ├─ operatorUi + labels + wizardSurfaces
       └─ (no flat-edit UI)

flat-edit page client
  ├─ warmOperatorWizardShell  (shared set above)
  └─ Promise.all(
       ensureFlatEditChromeReady,
       ensureFlatEditFormReady,
       ensureFlatEditPageReady
     )
```

## Verify

```bash
pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:file \
  test/wizard-create-warm-ownership.spec.ts \
  test/thin-shell-warm-ownership-matrix.spec.ts \
  test/thin-shell-flat-edit-chrome-capability.spec.ts \
  test/thin-shell-flat-edit-form-capability.spec.ts \
  test/thin-shell-flat-edit-page-capability.spec.ts \
  test/wave-i-9-create-wizard-async-plugin.spec.ts \
  test/wave-i-6-session-plugin-load.spec.ts \
  test/warm-operator-wizard-shell.spec.ts
```

Rebuild Denali after host-hook changes: `pnpm --filter @app-cloud/workspace-denali run build`.
